## What this licence covers, and what it does not

This licence covers **only this project's own work**:

- the PowerShell tooling in `scripts/`
- the global instructions template in `global/AGENTS.md`
- the documentation in `docs/`, `README.md`, `README.es.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `PLAN.md`, `CLAUDE.md`
- the machine-readable selection files in `manifest/`
- the **modifications** this project makes to the forked skills in `vendor/skills/`

MIT was chosen because it is the most permissive, maximally compatible licence for a toolkit
people are expected to fork and adapt, and because it places no restriction on combining this
tooling with the permissively licensed third-party skills it installs.

## Third-party content keeps its own licence

`vendor/skills/` contains **modified copies** of skills from other projects. Those remain the
copyright of their original authors and are used under **their own** licences. This repository does
not relicense them.

Every vendored skill carries a `PROVENANCE.md` recording the upstream repository, the exact commit,
the licence, the licence notice, and precisely what was modified. See also
[`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) for the full list and licence texts.

| Upstream project | Licence |
|---|---|
| `social-media-skills/skills` | MIT |
| `pbakaus/impeccable` | Apache-2.0 |
| `PracticalSwan/agent-skills` | MIT AND Apache-2.0 |

## Skills installed at install time, not redistributed here

Most selected skills are **not** included in this repository. They are fetched at install time from
a commit pinned in `manifest/skills.json`, and they remain under their own upstream licences. Those
include `jamditis/claude-skills-journalism` (MIT), `blacktwist/social-media-skills` (MIT),
`Nutlope/hallmark` (MIT), `affaan-m/ecc` (MIT), `PracticalSwan/agent-skills` (MIT AND Apache-2.0),
and `vercel-labs`-derived content.

One entry is recorded in `manifest/skills.json` with `licenseRisk:
ACCEPTED-BY-USER-2026-10-04`: `og-image`, whose upstream repository has **no licence file**.
Because it is fetched at install time and is **not** vendored here, this repository does not
redistribute it. Review that entry before installing on a machine you care about, and remove it from
the manifest if the licensing ambiguity is not acceptable to you.